WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:01.710
The year is 1939.

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:08.130
It’s the dead of night in Pingfang, a district
of the Harbin Prefecture in Japanese Imperial

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:09.540
Occupied China.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:14.780
A squadron of over a hundred Chinese rebels
led by Lieutenant Wang Wei, clutching Bergmann

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:20.400
MP 18 machine guns, hurry through the streets
towards their destination: The bioweapons

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:28.630
lab operated by Unit 731 and monstrous, terrifying
Japanese Surgeon General Shirō Ishii.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:31.970
It is a mission of liberation...and revenge.

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:36.960
If you know anything about Unit 731, just
hearing the name will send a chill down your

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:42.300
spine, just as it did for the Chinese soldiers
hoping to perform a surprise assault on the

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.620
Unit’s complex of horrors.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:48.690
Rumors had spread from the Chinese prisoners
of war taken there - and the knowledge of

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:53.830
the horrible things happening to their countrymen
inside that building made their blood boil

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:55.790
with white-hot fury.

00:00:55.790 --> 00:01:00.470
Their mission was simple: They would launch
an attack on the complex when the Unit least

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:05.690
expected it, save as many prisoners as they
could, while also taking revenge on as many

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:08.550
Unit Soldiers as they could get their hands
on.

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:13.170
But what the brave soldiers didn’t know
is that they were in for a battle they couldn’t

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.490
hope to win.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:19.140
Because what they were fighting was not, in
the traditional sense, human.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:26.300
They were about to go toe to toe with SCP-4007,
an elite group of anomalous Japanese super-soldiers

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.670
known as the Pingfang 5.

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:34.480
A name spoken in fear by their enemies and
victims, for what little time both remained

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:35.600
alive.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:39.690
The Chinese rebels were hiding in a stand
of trees outside the fortress, waiting for

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:45.240
the right moment to strike, when the Pingfang
5 suddenly beat them to the punch and descended

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.270
upon them.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:50.780
The plan was thrown into chaos when the trees
burst into flames without so much as a hint

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:52.890
of artillery being fired.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:57.100
The soldiers, all hardened men of war, began
to grow scared.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:03.060
But then they saw something even more terrifying
standing there amongst the flames: 1st Lieutenant

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:10.380
Mitsuo Kitano, also known as Lightning Bolt,
or SCP-4007-1 to the Foundation.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:15.130
One of his hands was wreathed in blue sparks
of electricity, and in the other, he wielded

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:17.569
a Type 14 Nambu pistol.

00:02:17.569 --> 00:02:22.700
Lieutenant Kitano continued his attack, using
his anomalous lightning to blow away soldier

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.130
after soldier.

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:28.660
When the shocked rebels tried to return fire,
they found that they couldn’t land a single

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:29.660
shot.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:31.860
Kitano dodged every bullet.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:36.780
The second wave of the assault came from behind
as the rebels tried to flee Kitano’s wrath.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:43.920
Private Takashi Honda, also known as The Ogre,
or SCP-4007-2, charged into the frey.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:49.500
He effortlessly wielded a Type 11 Machine
gun, and rained bullets down upon his unsuspecting

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:50.500
foes.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:54.850
They shot back at him, but the bullets seemed
to just bounce off of his skin.

00:02:54.850 --> 00:03:01.020
He wasn’t bothered by them in the slightest
- He just smiled, and continued firing.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:05.470
The rebels quickly realized that the whole
thing had been a trap, but what had given

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:06.470
them away?

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:11.060
As if on cue, one of their own soldiers turned
and began firing on his fellow soldiers with

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.050
his MP 18.

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:17.010
This man wasn’t a rebel - in fact, he wasn’t
even Chinese.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:21.410
It was Corporal Joichiro Ida, also known as
The Fox, or SCP-4007-3.

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:25.900
How could he have possibly infiltrated the
squadron?

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:29.910
The answer is simple: He’s an anomalously
brilliant liar.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:35.140
In fact, it’s impossible to not believe
a single thing that Corporal Ida says, making

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:38.050
him a true expert in espionage.

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:42.230
Not a single one of the other rebels ever
had a chance of sniffing him out before the

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:43.230
doomed mission.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:47.510
If this betrayal surprised them, then what
came next must have seemed like something

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:48.840
out of a nightmare.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:53.430
Lieutenant Wang Wei, the man who’d spearheaded
the entire mission, turned and began picking

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:55.980
off his own troops with his pistol.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:04:00.019
The surviving soldiers didn’t understand
- had the Lieutenant gone mad?

00:04:00.019 --> 00:04:05.090
They tried to shoot him, but just like the
others, he dodged effortlessly and continued

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:06.200
to murder them.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:10.050
That’s because he wasn’t Lieutenant Wang
Wei at all - Wei had been murdered in the

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:16.489
forest earlier that night, and replaced by
Private Teruo Nishimura, also known as SCP-4007-5,

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:19.229
or The Shapeshifter.

00:04:19.229 --> 00:04:25.039
The Pingfang Five had infiltrated and compromised
the mission from before it had even begun.

00:04:25.039 --> 00:04:27.599
They never even stood a chance.

00:04:27.599 --> 00:04:31.599
During the chaos of the massacre, a few of
the rebels had managed to escape, running

00:04:31.599 --> 00:04:34.229
through a nearby clearing into a thicket of
trees.

00:04:34.229 --> 00:04:39.249
If they could survive then perhaps they could
regroup and lead a second assault on another

00:04:39.249 --> 00:04:40.249
day.

00:04:40.249 --> 00:04:45.300
They had no hope of survival during a head-on
conflict with these anomalous supersoldiers,

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:48.719
they needed to get away and form a new strategy.

00:04:48.719 --> 00:04:52.770
But gunshots started ringing out through the
forest, tearing into their bodies and dropping

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:54.729
the men one by one.

00:04:54.729 --> 00:04:59.300
They tried to return fire, but they couldn’t
even see who was shooting them.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:03.319
It seemed to come from all directions; the
rebels’ dying thoughts were that the trees

00:05:03.319 --> 00:05:06.689
around them must have been crawling with Japanese
troops.

00:05:06.689 --> 00:05:11.830
The reality was even more frightening - it
was only one man.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:17.309
Private Shigeru Matsui, codenamed Smoke for
this ability to become invisible at will.

00:05:17.309 --> 00:05:23.949
To the Foundation, he’s known as SCP-4007-4,
the last member of the Pingfang Five - the

00:05:23.949 --> 00:05:28.189
deadliest troops in the entire Imperial Japanese
Army.

00:05:28.189 --> 00:05:32.789
But unlike many of the biological anomalies
catalogued by the SCP Foundation, the Pingfang

00:05:32.789 --> 00:05:36.249
Five were not born, they were made.

00:05:36.249 --> 00:05:42.349
In case you aren’t familiar with the infamous
Unit 731 and their horrifying complex in Pingfang,

00:05:42.349 --> 00:05:47.439
this unit was a secret department of the Japanese
army ordered into existence by Emperor Hirohito

00:05:47.439 --> 00:05:53.629
himself for one sinister purpose: Researching
chemical and biological weapons for the Japanese

00:05:53.629 --> 00:05:55.219
Imperial Army.

00:05:55.219 --> 00:05:59.599
Their leader, the Surgeon General Shirō Ishii,
was essentially given blanket permission to

00:05:59.599 --> 00:06:05.589
do whatever he deemed necessary in order to
achieve results for his Emperor and his nation.

00:06:05.589 --> 00:06:09.960
Ishii took that directive and ran with it,
unleashing pseudo-scientific evil on a level

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:13.960
matched only by the Nazi extermination camps
in Europe.

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:18.529
Experimental weapons and horrific diseases
were tested on captured Chinese civilians,

00:06:18.529 --> 00:06:21.689
political dissidents, and prisoners of war.

00:06:21.689 --> 00:06:26.529
Thousands of people met horrific ends through
execution, experimentation, and vivisection

00:06:26.529 --> 00:06:31.369
- which is the dissection of a subject that
is still very much alive.

00:06:31.369 --> 00:06:35.249
How does this relate to the Pingfang Five
and SCP-4007?

00:06:35.249 --> 00:06:41.050
It all comes back to a top secret project
overseen by Ishii himself: Project Shinka.

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:48.189
While Unit 731 was established in 1935, in
1937 they began working in collaboration with

00:06:48.189 --> 00:06:54.270
the Imperial Japanese Anomalous Matters Examination
Agency - Think of it as Imperial Japan’s

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:57.609
hypernationalist answer to the SCP Foundation.

00:06:57.609 --> 00:07:01.939
They had become aware of the existence of
anomalous individuals in Imperial Controlled

00:07:01.939 --> 00:07:06.839
territories, and General Ishii wanted to know
whether the powers manifested in these anomalous

00:07:06.839 --> 00:07:12.520
individuals could be induced in others through
forced organ removal and transplantation.

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:17.589
To test this hypothesis, Ishii had the Japanese
Secret Police round up anomalous individuals

00:07:17.589 --> 00:07:20.059
in Imperial Territory en masse.

00:07:20.059 --> 00:07:24.529
They were subjected to mass vivisections,
with the intention of isolating and removing

00:07:24.529 --> 00:07:26.469
anomalous organs.

00:07:26.469 --> 00:07:32.219
It was an act so positively genocidal in proportion
that East-Asia has statistically fewer anomalous

00:07:32.219 --> 00:07:35.129
humans than they statistically should to this
day.

00:07:35.129 --> 00:07:39.689
Ishii’s intention was to transplant the
organs into loyal volunteers from the Japanese

00:07:39.689 --> 00:07:44.289
military in order to create an unbeatable
military force.

00:07:44.289 --> 00:07:47.339
Perfect soldiers who would win the war for
them.

00:07:47.339 --> 00:07:51.749
The vast majority of these twisted experiments
were complete failures, leading to the higher

00:07:51.749 --> 00:07:57.409
ups at Unit 731 almost writing Project Shinka
off as a waste of time and canceling the whole

00:07:57.409 --> 00:08:03.979
thing, but there were soon five notable exceptions
- the very scary individuals you’ve already

00:08:03.979 --> 00:08:04.979
met.

00:08:04.979 --> 00:08:09.479
Not only did every member of the Pingfang
Five end up with a specific anomalous “superpower”

00:08:09.479 --> 00:08:14.539
as a result of the experiments, they also
experienced incredible, anomalous prowess

00:08:14.539 --> 00:08:15.819
across the board.

00:08:15.819 --> 00:08:21.090
Members of the Five boast extended longevity,
meaning they rarely show their age.

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:27.189
Enhanced physical abilities including faster
reflexes, incredible senses, and immense physical

00:08:27.189 --> 00:08:28.189
strength.

00:08:28.189 --> 00:08:33.220
They also appear to have advanced mental development,
displaying phenomenal tactical and strategic

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:38.870
reasoning, as well as the ability to effortlessly
learn, read, and speak multiple languages

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:43.599
like Japanese, English, Mandarin Chinese,
Russian, and German.

00:08:43.599 --> 00:08:47.850
Of course, Japan eventually lost the war,
but the Pingfang Five had no intentions of

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:49.550
ending their fight.

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:54.630
They continued their missions long after Japan
formally surrendered, causing chaos and violence

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:56.550
across East-Asia.

00:08:56.550 --> 00:09:00.880
After several unsuccessful engagements with
isolated members of the Pingfang Five - leading

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:06.090
to the deaths of many Foundation Agents and
civilians - The Foundation formed Mobile Task

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:12.370
Force Phi-51, aka MacArthur’s Dogs, an elite
group of operatives trained for the specific

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:15.590
mission of bringing down the Pingfang Five.

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:20.580
While the hunt rages on, three of the five
are already dead.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:26.620
SCP-4007-1, Mitsuo Kitano - the man who can
unleash bursts of electricity - met his end

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:29.230
in Burma in 1948.

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:35.050
During a procedure called Operation Smokehouse,
Phi-51 engaged Kitano in combat in the jungle.

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:39.060
As was one of his trademark techniques, he
attempted to use his electricity powers to

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:42.050
burn down the jungle and escape during the
chaos.

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:45.480
However, the Foundation operatives surrounded
and boxed him in.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:49.790
He couldn’t escape, and when the fires were
put out, he was found dead on the ground - the

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:53.400
apparent cause of death was smoke inhalation.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:10:00.330
SCP-4007-2, Takashi Honda - the man with the
bulletproof skin - died in 1957 in the Philippines.

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:05.720
Phi-51 engaged him in combat in a mission
dubbed Operation Homewrecker, which culminated

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:08.140
in them calling down an airstrike on him.

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:12.620
In the aftermath, Honda was found dead, but
his cause of death was determined as having

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:14.030
been.

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:22.050
And finally, SCP-4007-3, Joichiro Ida - the
man with the silver tongue - was found dead

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:24.750
a year later in 1958.

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:28.430
His corpse was discovered in his room in Guiyang,
Southern China.

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:32.290
He appeared to have been strangled to death,
and interestingly, there was evidence that

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:36.530
he’d tried to engage in a shootout with
his killer, but hadn’t succeeded in preventing

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:37.900
his own murder.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:42.470
All of these circumstances were somewhat mysterious,
but the Foundation didn’t investigate them

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:47.670
much further after the bodies were tagged
and bagged.

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:54.210
SCP-4007-5, Teruo Nishimura - the shapeshifter
- is still on the run today, while SCP-4007-4,

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:58.110
Shigeru Matsui - the invisible man - is doing
just the opposite.

00:10:58.110 --> 00:11:03.460
He lives in Sarawak, Malaysia, and works in
open cooperation with the SCP Foundation to

00:11:03.460 --> 00:11:07.340
help track down the fifth member of the Pingfang
Five.

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:11.580
Not much has changed in the 64 years since
the death of Joichiro Ida.

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:17.310
It seemed like the search for SCP-4007-4 had
gone cold, until a Foundation archival clerk

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:24.300
found something suspicious: The original paper
copy of the SCP-4007 document, which was dated

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:30.630
a year before the Foundation had supposedly
discovered the existence of SCP-4007.

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:34.960
As the archival worker dug further, they found
a number of unsettling discoveries that alter

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:38.310
the true meaning of SCP-4007.

00:11:38.310 --> 00:11:43.520
In the original paper documents, each dead
member of the Pingfang Five had organs missing.

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:48.470
And each subsequent member’s death involved
a power possessed by a former member: -2 was

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:53.870
electrocuted, and -3’s gun was useless,
as the killer had been wearing -2’s bulletproof

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:54.870
skin.

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:56.320
Who was behind this?

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:57.320
Why?

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:01.000
And most importantly of all: How had it all
been forgotten?

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:07.390
Through more digging, the Foundation discovered
the truth about SCP-4007-4: His powers weren’t

00:12:07.390 --> 00:12:10.110
invisibility, they were antimemetic.

00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:15.390
He can make people forget him at will, essentially
editing their memories, so he could do whatever

00:12:15.390 --> 00:12:21.310
he wanted without detection...Like, for example,
murdering his team members and stealing their

00:12:21.310 --> 00:12:22.310
powers.

00:12:22.310 --> 00:12:27.090
They even managed to find an archived letter
from 4 to 3, begging for his help in fighting

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:32.320
some kind of unknown monster - something that
would require their combined powers to face,

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:37.830
whether that ended up being as five separate
men or one man with all of their powers.

00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:43.660
This whole time, SCP-4007-4 had been playing
the Foundation like a fiddle.

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:48.570
Using their resources to help him track down
the final member of the Pingfang Five, to

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:54.240
recruit him into one final mission, or murder
him and steal his powers.

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:58.370
But that still leaves one question: What is
this mission?

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:00.310
What is this monster?

00:13:00.310 --> 00:13:03.910
The Foundation managed to find out, at least
partially.

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:08.410
They charted the death locations of each of
the three dead Pingfang members, and the living

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:13.370
location of SCP-4007-4, and discovered something
amazing…

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:19.340
Four of the five points on a perfect pentagon,
centering on the South China Sea.

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:25.020
The Foundation also estimated that the pentagon
would reveal the location of SCP-4007-5 at

00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:29.850
the final point, but his location isn’t
nearly as interesting as what resides at the

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:33.250
center of this massive geographical pentagon.

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:38.850
Foundation divers discovered huge numbers
of sunken Japanese battleships, downed planes,

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:41.580
and thousands of bones littering the seabed.

00:13:41.580 --> 00:13:46.640
Based on the damage to these vessels, it was
clear they hadn’t been shot or blown up.

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:52.550
No, they had been torn apart by something
obscenely huge and powerful underneath the

00:13:52.550 --> 00:13:53.550
water.

00:13:53.550 --> 00:13:59.170
The pentagon, a significant shape in sorcery,
is likely a massive, supernatural containment

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:05.040
ritual, keeping whatever unspeakable horror
is lurking under the ground there from escaping.

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:11.940
A containment ritual that could only be maintained
by five special individuals in five special

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:13.260
places…

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:18.211
It was in this moment that the Foundation
came upon a truly horrifying revelation: They

00:14:18.211 --> 00:14:21.370
had misjudged the intentions of Project Shinka.

00:14:21.370 --> 00:14:25.529
It was never about creating assets for the
war against the Allies, it was about a war

00:14:25.529 --> 00:14:30.710
against something else entirely, something
much more dangerous than and deadly than the

00:14:30.710 --> 00:14:32.260
squabbles between men.

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:35.140
It was about the entity that lurked below.

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:40.810
A creature that nobody understood, and that
no conventional weapon can fight.

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:46.690
And if the ritual is ever broken and the beast
is allowed to rise, the Pingfang Five will

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:49.850
be the very least of our problems.

00:14:49.850 --> 00:14:56.490
Now check out “SCP-001 - The Broken God
- Ouroboros Cycle” and “SCP-5545 - Mysterious

00:14:56.490 --> 00:15:01.470
Tunnels in Antarctica - Abnormality” for
more fascinating mysteries and rabbit holes

00:15:01.470 --> 00:15:03.350
from the SCP Foundation!

